      "note": "Note. Prey denotes the primary benthic-amphipod energy-density landscape; ice and vessel denote the May-July sea-ice accessibility and Automatic Identification System-derived vessel-exposure modifiers, respectively. Each scenario-year comprised 1,600 successful least-cost paths. Frequent-corridor cells were crossed by more than 5% of paths (Fs>0.05). In B, changes are calculated as the named scenario minus its reference scenario. Jaccard overlap ranges from 0 for no shared frequent-corridor cells to 1 for identical cell sets. Centroid displacement is the distance between the unweighted geographic centers of the paired frequent-corridor sets; positive northward components indicate that the first-named scenario lay north of its reference. Modeled path cost is a relative resistance-weighted distance, not measured whale energy expenditure. Displayed values are rounded; comparisons used unrounded values."
