      "note": "Note. Year-specific relative pelagic support was added only within observation-supported portions of the 2017 and 2018 landscapes. Prey denotes the primary benthic prey-only scenario. β controls the strength of added pelagic support, and β=0 reproduces the corresponding benthic baseline. The bounded complementary operator was prespecified as the primary formulation; the maximum and capped-additive operators respectively retained the larger support value or summed benthic and weighted pelagic support up to a maximum of 1. Changes and spatial comparisons are relative to the same scenario and year at β=0. Negative cost changes indicate lower modeled path cost, and positive cell-count changes indicate expansion of the frequent-corridor footprint (Fs>0.05). Panel B ranges span all four scenarios in both years. β is a sensitivity parameter, not an estimated conversion between benthic and pelagic prey energy."
